d junctions; map each\n    # chamber to the marker at its upper-left grid intersection, defaulting to fill color.\n    h,w=len(grid),len(grid[0])\n    # infer regular chamber pitches from repeated fill pattern\n    fill=max(set(v for row in grid for v in row), key=lambda v: sum(row.count(v) for row in grid))\n    rr=[i for i,row in enumerate(grid) if any(v!=fill for v in row)]\n    cc=[j for j in range(w) if any(grid[i][j]!=fill for i in range(h))]\n    # Colored separator crossings sit on repeated horizontal/vertical separator lines.\n    row_pitch=min(b-a for a,b in zip(rr,rr[1:]) if b-a>1)\n    col_pitch=min(b-a for a,b in zip(cc,cc[1:]) if b-a>1)\n    rows=[i for i in range(0,h,row_pitch)]\n    cols=[j for j in range(0,w,col_pitch)]\n    out=[]\n    for r in range(len(rows)-1):\n        line=[]\n        for c in range(len(cols)-1):\n            vals=[grid[rows[r]][cols[c]],grid[rows[r]][cols[c]+1] if cols[c]+1<w else fill]\n            vals=[v for v in vals if v!=fill]\n            line.append(vals[0] if vals else fill)\n        out.append(line)\n    return out\n'''\np.write_text(s)\nexec(s)\ng=[[2,2,2,2,7,2,2,7,2,2,7]]+[[0,2,0,0,2,0,0,2,0,0,2] for _ in range(7)]\ng += [[2,2,2,2,7,2,2,7,2,2,7]]+[[0,2,0,0,2,0,0,2,0,0,2] for _ in range(7)]\ng += [[2,7,2,2,7,2,2,8,2,2,8]]+[[0,2,0,0,2,0,0,2,0,0,2] for _ in range(7)]+[[2,7,2,2,7,2,2,8,2,2,8]]\nprint(len(g), transform(g))","t":1790702417.230691,"stored":["programs/task-84d28555.py"],"output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n\n  File \"<cell-4>\", line 31, in <module>\n    print(len(g), transform(g))\n                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\n  File \"<string>\", line 10, in transform\n\nValueError: min() arg is an empty sequence\n","error":true},{"type":"reasoning","text":"**Transforming output structure**\n\nI'm looking into the issue of producing the output. It seems like I need to display a 3x3 matrix using horizontal boundaries and column colors. Each cell marker should correspond to its position in the top boundary.